#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161681 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62aa30b-6bf5-5c06-bb1f-8269a6806368" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Discrete Probability Distributions"}] :question/id #uuid "ce0d131b-ec10-5895-942f-2bece346c152" :question/math-academy-id "e-10107" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n$l(\\theta) = 3\\ln\\theta + 4\\ln(1-\\theta)$,\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$, we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta$.\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dl}{dθ} &= \\frac{d}{dθ}(3\\ln θ + 4\\ln (1 - θ)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{θ} + \\frac{4}{1 - θ} \\cdot (-1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{θ} + \\frac{4}{θ - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{θ} + \\frac{4}{θ - 1} &= 0 \\\\\n(3(θ - 1) + 4θ)/(θ(θ - 1)) &= 0 \\\\\n3(θ - 1) + 4θ &= 0 \\\\\n7θ - 3 &= 0 \\\\\n7θ &= 3 \\\\\nθ &= \\frac{3}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is\n\n$$\n\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} = \\dfrac{3}{7}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161682 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162116 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78241be4-1db7-554c-a7ce-7532345f3f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Continuous Probability Distributions"}] :question/id #uuid "dd2ad84f-1fa2-5f7c-9af3-db9dce4b5133" :question/math-academy-id "e-10108" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent normal random variables $X_i\\sim N(\\theta,1)$ is\n$l(\\theta) = -6\\ln(2\\pi)-8.4 + 12.1\\, \\! \\theta - 6\\ \\! \\theta^2$,\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}$ for this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$, we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta$.\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dl}{dθ} &= \\frac{d}{dθ}(-6\\ln (2π) - 8.4 + 12.1θ - 6θ^{2}) \\\\\n&= 12.1 - 12θ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12.1 - 12θ &= 0 \\\\\n12θ &= 12.1 \\\\\n&= θ \\mid \\approx 1.008\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is\n\n$$\n\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} \\approx 1.008\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62aa30b-6bf5-5c06-bb1f-8269a6806368" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Discrete Probability Distributions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98fd53c6-1ce1-5e29-9342-f54498e4657c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159573} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b9c065-0650-5950-b74e-3025af0b5186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159574} {:answer/id #uuid "0b801eae-251d-5746-a091-62c984a643d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159575} {:answer/id #uuid "24d3dac4-c1cf-5041-9181-26b68f19294c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159576} {:answer/id #uuid "6c9dd77b-61c8-547a-ae1d-23baa0d22812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159577}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b2a9a069-b73f-5a6f-bd50-90972ad14ac2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159572}] :question/id #uuid "04a3c966-c6bc-5da3-b178-0b866e10e919" :question/math-academy-id "q-143525" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n$l(θ) = 5\\ln θ + \\ln (1 - θ)$,\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $θ^(^)$ from this sample?"}]}
